## ARENA ASSUMPTIONS ##
The arena is three-dimensional.
The arena has a floor.
The gradient of the ground is 0.0.
The arena has 4 walls.
The arena has 2 box obstacles.
The arena has 2 cylindrical obstacles.
## ROBOT ASSUMPTIONS ##
The robot is defined by a diagram.
The z-position of the base of the robot is constant.
The roll of the base of the robot is 0.0 rad.
The pitch of the base of the robot is 0.0 rad.
Initially the x-position of the robot is -2.56 m.
Initially the y-position of the robot is 0.0 m.
Initially the orientation of the robot is 0.0 rad.
Initially the velocity of the robot is 0.0 m/s.
Initially the angular velocity of the robot is 0.0 rad/s.
The logical time unit is 0.1 s.
The measurement period is 0.1 s.
